BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zine Making Workshop
DTSTART:20260821T200000Z
DTEND:20260821T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260815T055708Z
UID:11c91c57-eb63-5c5f-85b7-d974caaebb09
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Cycle Toronto Rec Hub for a hands-on Zine Makin
 g Workshop\, where you'll learn to fold\, cut\, and assemble a punk zine u
 sing the classic one-fold\, one-cut method. This session covers everything
  from the DIY ethos and history of zines to planning your content\, adding
  collage or drawings\, and finishing your creation. No experience or speci
 al tools are needed. Just bring your ideas\, and leave with new skills and
  a completed zine.\n\nDoors: 4 PM\n\nSession: 4:00-6:00 PM\n\n"SF punk zin
 es at Prelinger Library" by Lindsay Eyink is licensed under CC BY 2.0. (ht
 tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zine#/media/File:SF_punk_zines_at_Prelinger_Li
 brary.jpg) Source: Wikimedia Commons\nURL: https://www.cycleto.ca/zine_mak
 ing_workshop
LOCATION:Evergreen Brickworks\n550 Bayview Ave\n10\nToronto  ON M4W 3X8\nC
 A
URL:https://www.cycleto.ca/zine_making_workshop
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Election Townhall 2026
DTSTART:20260825T220000Z
DTEND:20260826T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260815T055709Z
UID:35e8dcf9-348b-5817-88d2-04d0042c8134
DESCRIPTION:Let’s talk about cycling!\n\nThis October\, you have the cha
 nce to send a message that streets are for people\, and that Toronto can't
  wait! Come chat with your neighbours about cycling and contribute to Cycl
 e Toronto’s election strategy.\nURL: https://www.cycleto.ca/2026election
 townhall
LOCATION:Swansea Townhall\n95 Lavinia Avenue\nToronto\, Ontario ON M6S 3H9
 \nCA
URL:https://www.cycleto.ca/2026electiontownhall
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rec Hub DIY
DTSTART:20260816T140000Z
DTEND:20260816T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260815T055709Z
UID:3ebe5225-8af7-5e70-b460-6c6bfcbc33c1
DESCRIPTION:(https://www.cycleto.ca/rec_hub)\n\nThe Cycle Toronto Rec Hub 
 at Evergreen Brick Works is a welcoming community space that takes the int
 imidation out of bike maintenance and repair.\n\nIF YOU'RE A TRAINED CYCLE
  TORONTO REC HUB VOLUNTEER\, SIGN UP FOR SUPPORT SHIFTS.\n\nOur friendly s
 taff and volunteers will help guide you through the basics to keep you rol
 ling. Even expert home mechanics are also welcome to use our facilities.\n
 \nDIY service is first come\, first serve.\n\nFind out more: (https://www.
 cycleto.ca/rec_hub) cycleto.ca/rec_hub\nURL: https://www.cycleto.ca/rec_hu
 b_diy_20260816
LOCATION:Rec Hub at Evergreen Brick Works\n550 Bayview Avenue\nToronto ON 
 M4W 3X8\nCA
URL:https://www.cycleto.ca/rec_hub_diy_20260816
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coffee Outside Group Ride
DTSTART:20260816T120000Z
DTEND:20260816T140000Z
DTSTAMP:20260815T055709Z
UID:41aaaca6-f17a-5239-ba5a-87b151e82a0f
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Coffee Outside\, a leisurely group ride along the 
 Don River trail system. We'll roll at a chill pace\, take in the greenery\
 , and stop for coffee and conversation at a scenic spot along the way. All
  bikes and all speeds are welcome. Just bring your mug\, your favourite br
 ew fixings\, and enjoy the morning.\n\nRide with GPS: https://ridewithgps.
 com/routes/56528830\n\nDoors: 8 AM\n\nSession: 8:00-10 AM\n\nLight snacks 
 provided\nURL: https://www.cycleto.ca/coffee_outside_group_ride
LOCATION:Woodborough Park\n1460 Castlefield Ave\n10\nToronto ON  M6M 1Y7\n
 CA
URL:https://www.cycleto.ca/coffee_outside_group_ride
END:VEVENT
